      "slug": "capsule-body-a95",
      "term": "Capsule body",
      "definition": "A shape with two rounded ends and a straight central tube. Work a sphere increase section at the start, then work straight rows for the tube length, then mirror the decrease section at the end. The two hemispheres are worked as part of the same piece, with no seam at either end."
    },
    {
      "slug": "wing-placement-a95",
      "term": "Wing placement",
      "definition": "The position at which wings are sewn relative to the body. For a dragonfly, all four wings attach at the shoulder: the point roughly one quarter of the body length behind the head. Upper wings angle slightly backward and outward; lower wings angle forward and outward. This mimics the resting pose of a real dragonfly."
    }
  ],
